---
import checkOutput from '../generated/check.txt?raw';

const lines = checkOutput.trimEnd().split('\n');
---

<section class="band">
  <div class="band-inner">
    <p class="rail"><b>eventgraph check</b>a real finding</p>
    <div>
      <h2>What a finding looks like.</h2>

      <p class="lede">
        A takeaway app takes an order, charges the card, and shows the customer
        a tracking screen. The payment code is correct. The tracking screen is
        correct. And when a payment is refused, that fact reaches neither — so
        the customer waits for an order that is never coming.
      </p>

      <p>
        Nothing in either file is wrong, which is why this survives review. It
        is only visible once both halves are in the same model: the event exists,
        and no edge leaves it.
      </p>

      <figure class="stub">
        <svg viewBox="0 8 620 104" role="img" aria-label="A command produces an event, and the edge leaving that event ends in nothing.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="head" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path d="M0,1 L9,5 L0,9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" />
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <g class="n n1">
            <text class="kind" x="8" y="30" fill="var(--command)">command</text>
            <rect x="8" y="40" width="152" height="46" rx="2" />
            <text class="id" x="24" y="69">pay-order</text>
          </g>

          <g class="edge e1">
            <line x1="162" y1="63" x2="216" y2="63" marker-end="url(#head)" />
          </g>

          <g class="n n2">
            <text class="kind" x="222" y="30" fill="var(--event)">event</text>
            <rect x="222" y="40" width="182" height="46" rx="2" />
            <text class="id" x="238" y="69">payment-refused</text>
          </g>

          <g class="edge e2 dangling">
            <line x1="406" y1="63" x2="556" y2="63" stroke-dasharray="5 5" />
            <circle cx="566" cy="63" r="8" />
          </g>

          <text class="void" x="586" y="68">?</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>
          Every other edge in this model lands on something. This one has no
          read-model to project into and no policy to trigger.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="terminal" role="group" aria-label="Output of eventgraph check">
        <div class="prompt"><span class="sigil">$</span> eventgraph check</div>
        <pre>{lines.map(line => <span>{line || ' '}{'\n'}</span>)}</pre>
      </div>

      <p class="footnote">
        That output is not a mock-up. It is regenerated from <code>site/demo</code> every
        time this page is built, so a rule whose wording changes cannot leave a
        stale claim here.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .lede {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .stub {
    margin: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem) 0;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .stub svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .stub .kind {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .stub .id {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 15px;
    fill: var(--ink);
  }

  .stub rect {
    fill: var(--wall-raised);
    stroke: var(--rule-strong);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .stub .n1 rect { stroke: var(--command); }
  .stub .n2 rect { stroke: var(--event); }

  .stub .edge line {
    stroke: var(--ink-soft);
    stroke-width: 1.75;
  }

  .stub .dangling line { stroke: var(--error); }

  .stub .dangling circle {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--error);
    stroke-width: 1.75;
    stroke-dasharray: 3 4;
  }

  .stub .void {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 17px;
    fill: var(--error);
  }

  .stub figcaption {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .terminal {
    max-width: 54rem;
  }

  .prompt {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    background: var(--wall-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 0;
    border-radius: 3px 3px 0 0;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.35rem;
  }

  .sigil {
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
  }

  .terminal pre {
    border-radius: 0 0 3px 3px;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }

  .footnote {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 1.1rem 0 0;
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
</style>
